   "moduleId": "migration-modernization",
   "question": "A company has an existing on-premises three-tier web application. The Linux web servers serve content from a centralized file share on a NAS server because the content is refreshed several times a day from various sources. The existing infrastructure is not optimized and the company would like to move to AWS in order to gain the ability to scale resources up and down in response to load. On-premises and AWS resources are connected using AWS Direct Connect.  How can the company migrate the web infrastructure to AWS without delaying the content refresh process?",
