   "question": "A company is migrating an on-premises content management system (CMS) to AWS Fargate. The company uses the CMS for blog posts that include text, images, and videos. The company has observed that traffic to blog posts drops by more than 80% after the posts are more than 30 days old. The CMS runs on multiple VMs and stores application state on disk. This application state is shared across all instances across multiple Availability Zones. Images and other media are stored on a separate NFS file share. The company needs to reduce the costs of the existing solution while minimizing the impact on performance.  Which combination of steps will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively? (Select TWO.)",
