   "id": "sapc02-q934",
   "number": 374,
   "topic": "Identifying and cheapening unused DynamoDB tables",
   "moduleId": "continuous-improvement",
   "question": "A company has several Amazon DynamoDB tables in an AWS Region. Each table has more than 100,000 records and was created with default table settings.  To reduce costs, the company needs to identify unused tables. However, the company must maintain the availability and current performance capability of the tables in case the company must use the tables in the future.  Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Select THREE.)",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "text": "In Amazon CloudWatch, graph the sum of the ReadThrottleEvents metric and the sum of the WriteThrottleEvents metric for each table over a period of 1 month."
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "text": "In Amazon CloudWatch, graph the sum of the ConsumedReadCapacityUnits metric and the sum of the ConsumedWriteCapacityUnits metric for each table over a period of 1 month."
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "text": "Change the provisioned RCUs to 1 for the unused tables. Change the provisioned WCUs to 1 for the unused tables."
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "text": "Change the capacity mode of the unused tables to on-demand mode."
    },
    {
     "key": "E",
     "text": "Change the table class of the unused tables to DynamoDB Standard-Infrequent Access (DynamoDB Standard-IA)."
    },
    {
     "key": "F",
     "text": "Purchase a reserved capacity of 1 RCU and 1 WCU for each unused table."
    }
   ],
   "answer": "BDE",
   "explanation": "Consumed read/write capacity metrics show whether a table does any work, on-demand mode stops charging for idle provisioned throughput while keeping capacity available, and Standard-IA cuts storage cost with identical performance. Throttle metrics (A) do not show usage, and 1 RCU/WCU (C) or reserved capacity (F) would hurt performance or still pay for idle capacity.",
   "reference": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/metrics-dimensions.html",
   "images": [],
   "interactive": null,
   "verified": 2,
   "imported": true,
   "auditVerdict": "verified",
   "auditLabel": "Verified against AWS documentation",
   "auditNote": "Standard-IA raises per-request cost; fine for idle tables.",
