   "question": "A company hosts a large application on AWS. The application consists of several containerized microservices that run in Amazon ECS containers with the AWS Fargate launch type. The microservices store data in an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster that consists of one DB instance. The company requires all data to reside in a single AWS Region. During a recent application update, one microservice increased the number of read operations. The increase had a major performance impact on the database, causing several microservices’ write operations to fail. The company must address the performance issues and prevent negative impacts on write operations in the future.  Which solution will meet these requirements?",
