   "question": "A company has an organization in AWS Organizations. In a linked AWS account, the company has Amazon EC2 instances that are running for different projects. The company uses cost allocation tags for the EC2 instances and the Amazon EBS volumes to map the resources to the different projects. After a project is finished, the company terminates the EC2 instances and the EBS volumes. Occasionally, EC2 instances and EBS volumes are not tagged. In these cases, the company struggles to map the resources to the correct project. A solutions architect must create an SCP to prevent the creation of EC2 instances and EBS volumes without the project tags.  Which SCP will meet these requirements?",
