   "question": "A company runs an application in a primary AWS Region and maintains a pilot light disaster recovery (DR) environment in a secondary Region. The company uses an organization in AWS Organizations with all features enabled to manage its cloud environment. The company uses AWS CloudFormation to deploy resources to both Regions.  During a test, the company cannot fail over to the DR Region within the company's RTO target of 60 minutes because the DR Region's infrastructure has experienced configuration drift. The company observes drift in security groups, AMI versions, and application configurations. The configuration drift between the two Regions causes a delay of 30 to 45 minutes to scale up to production levels.  The company needs an automated solution to prevent configuration drift so the company can fail over to the DR Region within the target RTO.  Which solution will meet this requirement?",
