   "moduleId": "new-solutions",
   "question": "A company is launching a web-based application in multiple regions around the world The application consists of both static content stored in a private Amazon S3 bucket and dyna ECS containers behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) The company requires that the static and dynamic application content be accessible through Amazon CloudFront only  Which combination of steps should a solutions architect recommend to restrict direct content access to CloudFront? (Select THREE)",
