   "moduleId": "new-solutions",
   "question": "A company has built a high performance computing (HPC) cluster in AWS for a tightly coupled workload that generates a large number of shared files stored in Amazon EFS. The cluster was performing well when the number of Amazon EC2 instances in the cluster was 100.  However, when the company increased the cluster size to 1,000 EC2 instances, overall performance was well below expectations Which collection of design choices should a solutions architect make to achieve the maximum performance from the HPC cluster? (Select THREE.)",
